% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% What the model covers: the goods of the chapter's families, and the forms
% of precious metal, waste and dust that carry precious metal or gems.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% the model covers the articles, gems and coin of Chapter 71
rule precious_scope_family:
a good is a good the model describes
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of chapter seventy-one goods.

% the model covers precious metal in a form of Additional U.S. note 1, and
% precious metal waste and scrap
rule precious_scope_metal:
a good is a good the model describes
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is a form of metal a form
    and the good contains precious metal beyond minor constituents.

% the model covers dust and powder of gems
rule precious_scope_dust:
a good is a good the model describes
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is in [dust, powder]
    and the good incorporates pearls or stones.

jewelry is a family of chapter seventy-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XIV and Chapter 71, confer "the expression \"articles of jewelry\" means".
personal article is a family of chapter seventy-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XIV and Chapter 71, confer "Articles of personal use of a kind normally carried in the pocket, in the handbag or on the person".
jewelry part is a family of chapter seventy-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XIV and Chapter 71, confer "Articles of jewelry and parts thereof, of precious metal or of metal clad with precious metal".
goldsmiths ware is a family of chapter seventy-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XIV and Chapter 71, confer "the expression \"articles of goldsmiths' or silversmiths' wares\" includes such articles as".
loose gem is a family of chapter seventy-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XIV and Chapter 71, confer "whether or not worked or graded but not strung, mounted or set".
coin is a family of chapter seventy-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XIV and Chapter 71, confer "Coin (other than gold coin), not being legal tender".

